\label{sec:reg-uni}
Suppose that $G$ is almost simple. Let $G^{{\mathrm{reg}}, \text{uni}}$ be the set of regular unipotent elements in $G$. Then $$G^{{\mathrm{reg}}, \text{uni}} \cap G_{\geqslant 0}=\bigsqcup_{w \in W, \operatorname{supp}(w)=I} U^+_{w, >0} \sqcup \sqcup_{w \in W, \operatorname{supp}(w)=I} U^-_{w, >0}.$$

In particular, $G^{{\mathrm{reg}}, \text{uni}} \cap G_{\geqslant 0}$ has two connected components and they are dense in the unipotent radical of two opposite Borel subgroups $B^+$ and $B^-$.

\label{conj}
Assume that $G$ is simply laced. Let $g \in G_{\geqslant 0}$ and $H=Z_G(g_s)$. Then there exists a weak pinning $\underline{\mathbf P_H}$ of $H$ such that 

\begin{enumerate}
    \item $g_u \in H_{\underline{\mathbf P_H}, \geqslant 0}$; 

    \item $V(g, c_M)_{\underline{\mathbf P_H}, \geqslant 0}=V(g, c_M) \cap V_{\geqslant 0}$ for any irreducible representation $V$ of $G$. 
\end{enumerate}
